1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,056
Orchard Core modules send messages through three services:

2
00:00:05,056 --> 00:00:07,338
email, SMS, and notifications.

3
00:00:07,338 --> 00:00:11,837
In this video, you inject each service in your own module, send a

4
00:00:11,837 --> 00:00:16,020
message, check the result, and register a notification type.

5
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:25,841
The Email module provides I Email Service, the SMS module provides I SMS

6
00:00:25,841 --> 00:00:30,928
Service, and the Notifications module provides I Notification Service.

7
00:00:30,928 --> 00:00:34,610
You inject the one you need, and call Send Async.

8
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:37,464
Email and SMS return a Result.

9
00:00:37,464 --> 00:00:40,738
Check Succeeded, and read Errors when it is false.

10
00:00:40,738 --> 00:00:46,057
A notification returns a Notification Send Result, which counts the methods that sent

11
00:00:46,057 --> 00:00:48,220
it and the methods that failed.

12
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:53,949
Declare the features your module uses in its manifest, and the Features page

13
00:00:53,949 --> 00:00:56,681
enables them together with your module.

14
00:00:56,681 --> 00:01:03,420
Email Notifications and SMS Notifications are separate features, and each one adds a notification method.

15
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:11,434
Inject I Email Service in the class that sends the message.

16
00:01:11,434 --> 00:01:16,069
The Email module registers it, so the constructor is all your code needs.

17
00:01:16,069 --> 00:01:19,120
The site settings select the default provider.

18
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:22,159
Create a Mail Message.

19
00:01:22,159 --> 00:01:29,025
To, Cc, and Bcc take one or more addresses, separated by commas or semicolons.

20
00:01:29,025 --> 00:01:33,930
Set a Subject, and an Html Body, a Text Body, or both.

21
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:38,384
Send Async returns a Result, so check Succeeded.

22
00:01:38,384 --> 00:01:41,676
The service validates every address first.

23
00:01:41,676 --> 00:01:46,545
It requires at least one recipient in To, Cc, or Bcc, and reports

24
00:01:46,545 --> 00:01:49,220
problems as errors in the result.

25
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:55,283
Pass the technical name of a provider, such as SMTP, to skip the default provider.

26
00:01:55,283 --> 00:01:58,603
A name that no provider uses throws an exception.

27
00:01:58,603 --> 00:02:02,950
A shorter overload takes the recipient, the subject, and the body.

28
00:02:07,150 --> 00:02:09,287
I SMS Service works the same way.

29
00:02:09,287 --> 00:02:13,561
Create an SMS Message with the phone number in To, including the country

30
00:02:13,561 --> 00:02:15,370
code, and the text in Body.

31
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:16,630
From is optional:

32
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:19,370
the provider uses its own number when empty.

33
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,655
I SMS Service has no provider argument.

34
00:02:22,655 --> 00:02:26,543
It uses the default SMS provider that the site settings select.

35
00:02:26,543 --> 00:02:29,980
A shorter overload takes the phone number and the text.

36
00:02:30,730 --> 00:02:32,810
Providers validate differently.

37
00:02:32,810 --> 00:02:37,981
The Azure Communication Services provider returns a failed result for a missing number

38
00:02:37,981 --> 00:02:41,297
or body, but the Twilio provider throws an exception.

39
00:02:41,297 --> 00:02:44,220
Check the number and the body before you send.

40
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:49,573
While you develop, the Log provider writes each message to the application log

41
00:02:49,573 --> 00:02:51,107
instead of sending it.

42
00:02:51,107 --> 00:02:55,491
It is registered only in the Development environment, and you select it as

43
00:02:55,491 --> 00:02:57,190
the default SMS provider.

44
00:03:01,390 --> 00:03:05,910
A notification is stored in the notification center of a user, then sent

45
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:09,098
with each notification method that user receives.

46
00:03:09,098 --> 00:03:13,270
Inject I Notification Service, and pass the user as a User object.

47
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:16,473
Build a Notification Message.

48
00:03:16,473 --> 00:03:21,378
The Subject is plain text, and the Summary can hold Html markup.

49
00:03:21,378 --> 00:03:26,214
Email and SMS send the Text Body, and email sends the Html Body

50
00:03:26,214 --> 00:03:31,540
instead when Is Html Preferred is true and the Html Body is not empty.

51
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:39,401
Send Async returns a Notification Send Result, whose Notification property is the stored notification.

52
00:03:39,401 --> 00:03:45,458
Status is Success, Partially Successful, Failed, or None when no method was available.

53
00:03:45,458 --> 00:03:47,960
Errors says why a method failed.

54
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:53,593
Which methods run depends on the enabled features and the preferences of the user.

55
00:03:53,593 --> 00:03:57,810
A method that cannot reach the user, such as email without an address,

56
00:03:57,810 --> 00:04:01,860
fails alone, and the notification stays in the notification center.

57
00:04:02,610 --> 00:04:05,486
Do not confuse notifications with I Notifier.

58
00:04:05,486 --> 00:04:09,434
I Notifier shows a short message in the page the user sees next,

59
00:04:09,434 --> 00:04:11,803
such as a confirmation after a save.

60
00:04:11,803 --> 00:04:14,510
It is not kept in the notification center.

61
00:04:18,710 --> 00:04:21,690
A type names the notifications of your module.

62
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:27,363
Register it in your startup with Add Notification Type, a technical name, and a display name.

63
00:04:27,363 --> 00:04:31,890
Keep the technical name in a constant, since each notification stores it.

64
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:38,325
The display name labels the notifications and fills the Type filter of the notification center.

65
00:04:38,325 --> 00:04:42,828
It also appears in the preferences of each user when a notification method

66
00:04:42,828 --> 00:04:47,500
is enabled, and Disabled Methods turns a method off by default for this type.

67
00:04:48,250 --> 00:04:52,834
On the message, set the Type, a Reference Id for the record the

68
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:57,817
notification is about, and a Url that opens when the user selects it.

69
00:04:57,817 --> 00:05:02,600
The type is limited to 64 characters, and the reference id to 255.

70
00:05:03,350 --> 00:05:06,999
When the record changes, inject I Notification Manager.

71
00:05:06,999 --> 00:05:11,425
Delete, mark as read, or list the notifications with a filter on the

72
00:05:11,425 --> 00:05:13,997
user, the type, and the reference id.

73
00:05:13,997 --> 00:05:16,330
At least one of them is required.

74
00:05:20,530 --> 00:05:25,006
To add a provider, implement I Email Provider or I SMS Provider, and

75
00:05:25,006 --> 00:05:27,425
register it with a technical name.

76
00:05:27,425 --> 00:05:32,626
An enabled provider appears in the default provider list, and email also accepts

77
00:05:32,626 --> 00:05:34,380
its name in Send Async.

78
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:39,499
A notification method implements I Notification Method Provider.

79
00:05:39,499 --> 00:05:44,867
Register it as a scoped service, and it appears in the preferences of each user.

80
00:05:44,867 --> 00:05:50,110
To follow each email as it is sent or fails, implement I Email Service Events.

81
00:05:52,110 --> 00:05:55,851
That's how a module sends email, SMS, and notifications:

82
00:05:55,851 --> 00:06:01,101
inject the service, check its result, and register a type for your notifications.

83
00:06:01,101 --> 00:06:02,670
Thanks for watching.

